rmat="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>APPLIED MATERIALS INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNAGA, YASUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIURA, RYUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, KOICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUNAGA YASUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIURA RYUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNAGA, YASUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIURA, RYUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>For ion implantation of a wafer, a wafer transfer robot carries a wafer from a wafer cassette onto the surface of an elastic sheet of a wafer holder. After the ion implantation, the wafer transfer robot removes the wafer from the wafer holder and returns it to the wafer cassette. At this time, if no more wafers to be processed exist in the loading lock chamber, a dummy wafer in a wafer cassette is carried to the surface of the elastic sheet of the wafer holder, so that the surface of the elastic sheet is protected from contaminants.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un procédé d'implantation ionique sur une tranche. Selon ce procédé, un robot de transfert de tranches transporte une cassette de tranches sur la surface d'une feuille élastique d'un porte-tranche. Après implantation ionique, le robot de transfert retire la tranche du porte-tranche et la replace dans la cassette. A ce moment, s'il n'y a plus de tranches à traiter dans la chambre de chargement/verrouillage, une tranche factice située dans la cassette de tranches est transportée sur la surface de la feuille élastique du porte-tranche de manière à protéger la surface de la dite feuille contre les substances contaminantes.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>